    "type": "question",
    "label": "65",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\left(\\frac{5x^2}{y^4}\\right)^{-2}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{y^8}{25x^4}$, $x,y\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{5x^2}{y^4}\\right)^{-2}&=\\left(\\frac{y^4}{5x^2}\\right)^2\\\\\\left(\\frac{5x^2}{y^4}\\right)^{-2}&=\\frac{y^8}{25x^4}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator and negative power require $x,y\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
